Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 05:47:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Send the websites' name in emails, never the server's IP
 address

The login email, the panel's Email their login, resend-credentials.php
and add-student.sh all took the websites' address straight from
server_url in /etc/5cs045/smtp_config.php. On this server that still
holds the private IP from before the names existed, so students were
sent https://10.80.0.250/~name/... links, which mean nothing off campus
and only redirect to the student name on campus.

They now all go through one helper, student_site_url(): it uses
server_url only when it is a name, and otherwise
https://fullstack-student.heraldcollege.edu.np, the only name the
websites answer on. The sign-up link follows the same rule for
signup_url. Nothing needs changing in smtp_config.php, and the panel
shows the same address the emails use.

The config template now holds the two real addresses instead of
example.edu ones, so a fresh install cannot email links to a made-up
site. The health check fails if login details give an IP address.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
